    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "that makes sense. i'm definitely seeing some of that stunted growth in the patchy areas. quick question though, since portland can be so rainy and damp, is it possible for the soil just to \"hold onto\" the nutrients too much or for them to be unavailable even if i'm fertilizing? i just want to make sure i'm not wasting money if the nutrients are there but the grass just isn't grabbing them.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
